{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/optics/lenses-mirrors/","source":"students/subjects/physics/optics/lenses-mirrors.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Lenses & Mirrors | Physics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-6\"><a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/optics/\" class=\"text-blue-600\">← Back to Optics</a></nav>\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n      <h1 class=\"text-2xl font-bold mb-2\">Lenses &amp; Mirrors</h1>\n      <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Lens formula: 1/f = 1/u + 1/v. Sign conventions: convex has positive focal length, concave negative (simple treatment here).</p>\n      <section class=\"mb-4\">\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Practice</h2>\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal list-inside\">\n          <li>An object is 30 cm from a convex lens of focal length 10 cm. Find image distance.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </section>\n      <section>\n        <h2 class=\"font-semibold\">Solution</h2>\n        <p>1/v = 1/f − 1/u = 1/10 − 1/30 = (3−1)/30 = 2/30 → v = 15 cm.</p>\n      </section>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif} .content-card{-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(16px);backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.8);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.06);} .diagram{max-width:100%;height:auto}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}